// us.irs.rev_proc_87_56 — IRS Rev. Proc. 87-56: class lives and recovery
// periods of 26 U.S.C. §168 (1987-2 C.B. 674–687).
//
// WHY A PACKAGE. The (e)/(g)/(h)/(i) rows of §168 read class life and
// recovery periods from outside the statute: the class-life key is the
// Rev. Proc. 87-56 asset-class table (§168(i)(1) points at pre-1986
// §167(m) lives; 87-56 prescribes them for post-1986 property). Owners need
// the table contract «asset class → (class life, printed GDS/ADS recovery)»
// plus anchored rows, not the 2264-page Bulletin. No row names concrete
// classes: the full table is pinned (133 classes + assigned property A–E).
//
// WHAT IT HOLDS (phase 1, still rule-less). `sources/rp-87-56/en.txt` —
// the pinned `pdftotext -layout` extraction of 1987-2 C.B. 674–687
// (PINNED_UNOFFICIAL_COPY; the granule PDF bytes live in
// `docs/foundations/us-irc/raw/cb1987/`, PINNED_OFFICIAL_BYTES).
// `sources.law` — source/edition/publication + one fragment per asset class
// (id `RP8756_<code>`) + curated fragments (SEC.2 definition, SEC.4
// prescription, reprint note, A–E table, footnotes).
// `sources/tables/rp8756-life.lawtable.json` (class lives, incl. 00.12 per
// SEC.4.02 prescription), `rp8756-gds-recovery-printed` (printed GDS cells
// only — blank cells are absent, GDS otherwise derives from the statute),
// `rp8756-ads-recovery` (printed ADS cells). All three `total: false`:
// absence of a row is data (no printed value / later amendments unknown),
// never a zero. Everything derived is GENERATED by
// `corpus/tools/sources/sync/sync_us_irs_rev_proc_87_56_87_57.py`, never
// hand-edited. No rules: the value enters the case as a case fact
// (`asset_class_life_years` in `us.irc.deductions`). Same shape as
// `us.irs.rev_rul_afr`.
//
// LAYOUT NOTE. `check_laws_tree` §3.5 derives `us/rev-proc-87-56` from
// jurisdiction US + instrument guidance (`us.irs` is not a GROUP_BY_NAME_PREFIX
// group): the package name keeps the `irs` issuer segment, the path does not.
//
// OUT OF SCOPE. Rev. Proc. 88-22 (reflected in this reprint; not pinned
// separately); later amendments to the 87-56 classes, if any (flagged in
// provenance anomalies); the 87-57 percent tables (sibling package
// `us.irs.rev_proc_87_57`).
//
// REPRINT NOTE. The Bulletin prints 87-56 «as reprinted here ... reflects
// the changes effected by Rev. Proc. 88-22, 1988-18 I.R.B.» — the pinned
// slice IS 87-56+88-22 (fragment `RP8756_REPRINT_8822`).

language "law.core" version "0.2";
package us.irs.rev_proc_87_56 version "0.1.1";
namespace "urn:us:irs:rev_proc_87_56:clir";
